{%- comment -%}
  The pixel heart from the carton's inside flap.

  It replaced three kolams here. A kolam is ONE connected lattice — a grid of
  dots with a single unbroken line looping through all of them — and three copies
  of one four-petal motif in a row is not that; it read as clip art, and the pale
  pulli at that size read as dirt on the pink.

  The heart is the mark the pack actually uses above "Hey, chum!", and it is
  built from square cells, so it shares a vocabulary with the pixel-stepped teeth
  directly beneath it. The flowers never did.

  Parameters
    tone   fill colour token. Default '--c-surface'.
    size   rendered width in px. Default 96.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign tone = tone | default: '--c-surface' -%}
{%- assign size = size | default: 96 -%}
<svg class="gc-pixel-heart" width="{{ size }}" viewBox="0 0 11 10" fill="var({{ tone }})"
     aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" role="presentation" shape-rendering="crispEdges">
    <rect x="2" y="0" width="2" height="1"/>
    <rect x="7" y="0" width="2" height="1"/>
    <rect x="1" y="1" width="4" height="1"/>
    <rect x="6" y="1" width="4" height="1"/>
    <rect x="0" y="2" width="11" height="1"/>
    <rect x="0" y="3" width="11" height="1"/>
    <rect x="0" y="4" width="11" height="1"/>
    <rect x="1" y="5" width="9" height="1"/>
    <rect x="2" y="6" width="7" height="1"/>
    <rect x="3" y="7" width="5" height="1"/>
    <rect x="4" y="8" width="3" height="1"/>
    <rect x="5" y="9" width="1" height="1"/>
</svg>
